# Test: deleting a created peer frees the BGP role its OPEN declared
# VALIDATES: create bgp peer against a router whose OPEN says Role customer,
#            then delete bgp peer: bgp-role drops that learned role before the
#            delete returns, though no attach block names bgp-role. A peer
#            created again at the same address, against a router whose OPEN
#            carries no Role, establishes and is not reported as withdrawing
#            the role only the deleted peer advertised.
# PREVENTS: the deleted peer's role being kept for the process life and read by
#           the next peer of that name (resolvePeerRole prefers it to the
#           configured complement).
# The scenario: internal/test/fixture/role_learned_cleared_fixture.go. It starts
# the two routers itself, one after the other on 127.0.0.2, because one test
# peer sends the same OPEN on every connection.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.log.bgp.role:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external role-cleared-driver {
		run "le test fixture plugin/role-learned-cleared-on-peer-delete $PORT"
		encoder json
	}
}

bgp {
	router-id 1.2.3.4
	session {
		asn {
			local 65000
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze --plugin ze.bgp-role -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=60s
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the created peer established with Role customer
expect=stderr:pattern=learned role dropped: peer removed.*previous-role=customer
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the created peer was deleted
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the peer created again established with no Role
reject=stderr:contains=role capability withdrawn
expect=exit:code=0
